  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "14ccda568e211f8f4474c196f8db6c1e66f487d4d1a7e917e8fa5f8065fe1ad9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-14ccda568e21-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The petitioner argues that an offense renders an alien inadmissible if the immigration judge finds the offense makes the alien inadmissible at the removal hearing that triggers the stop\u2011time rule."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Unikowski",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "14ccda568e211f8f4474c196f8db6c1e66f487d4d1a7e917e8fa5f8065fe1ad9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-14ccda568e21-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Unikowski, the petitioner contends that Congress intended the statute to allow eligibility for discretionary relief, noting that the offense at issue was not serious enough to make the alien deportable and that Congress left the door open for cancellation of removal."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Unikowski",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "14ccda568e211f8f4474c196f8db6c1e66f487d4d1a7e917e8fa5f8065fe1ad9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-14ccda568e21-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 26,
                "start": 26
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Unikowski, the petitioner further asserts that crimes that make the alien deportable do not foreclose eligibility for cancellation of removal because Congress expressly left that possibility open."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "14ccda568e211f8f4474c196f8db6c1e66f487d4d1a7e917e8fa5f8065fe1ad9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-14ccda568e21-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 46,
                "start": 46
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The petitioner maintains that the word \u201cinadmissible\u201d should have a consistent meaning throughout the Immigration and Nationality Act."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Government",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "14ccda568e211f8f4474c196f8db6c1e66f487d4d1a7e917e8fa5f8065fe1ad9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-14ccda568e21-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Government, the government concedes that the terms \u201cinadmissible\u201d and \u201cremovable\u201d in the stop\u2011time rule refer to the charge at the removal proceeding, not to the alien\u2019s status."
        }
      ],
